Because monsters don't move when you're not on that level I
am more aggressive about a stash - I like to put mine close to
the down stairs.  When I climb up to my stash I appear on the
down stairs close to my stash so monsters do not have time
to get close ot it.  Then I descend again and I don't take long
getting to the stairs.

Sometimes I combine this strategy with burned Elbereth or
containers, sometimes not.

> Other than being looted
> by NPCs, is my pile of goodies in any danger of disappearing or degrading
> over time?

Burried items rot so don't put your stash in a pit.  Flooded items
rust so don't put your stash in the same room as a sink or
fountain.  Corpses not in an ice box go bad so if you want to
keep fresh corpses use an ice box - I prefer tins.

